# ActuNode broker permissions (D-23). Anything not allowed here is denied.
#
# Users: actunode-backend, tools, healthcheck, and one user per robot named <manufacturer>.<serial>
# (simulated robots ActuNode.robot_01 ... ActuNode.robot_50; real robots added with
# `docker compose run --rm mqtt-init add-robot <manufacturer> <serial>`). Topics assume the interface
# name "uagv" (ACTUNODE_VDA_INTERFACE).

# Backend: sends orders and failure commands, replays recordings (publishes robot topics), reads all.
user actunode-backend
topic readwrite uagv/#
topic readwrite actunode/#
# The broker's statistics (heap, clients, stored and dropped messages) for /api/metrics (D-57).
topic read $SYS/broker/#

# People and their tools (mosquitto_sub, MQTT Explorer): read only.
user tools
topic read uagv/#
topic read actunode/#

# Docker health check of the broker.
user healthcheck
topic read $SYS/broker/uptime

# Robots: mqtt-init appends one block per robot login (<manufacturer>.<serial>, D-28) to a copy of
# this file in the secrets volume; that copy is what the broker loads. Each robot may publish only its
# own robot-to-master topics and read only its own commands, under its own manufacturer and serial
# (VDA major versions v2 and v3). A robot can never publish as another robot or send orders.
# Master controls (outside fleet managers, D-47) log in as master@<name>, added with
# `docker compose run --rm mqtt-init add-master <name> [<manufacturer> ...]`: they may send commands to those
# manufacturers' robots and read their traffic; they cannot publish robot topics or reach actunode/#.
